From 73f91dc66848efc3e52609bd511fb71f09c7e1e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 04:23:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] fix(api): list every audit action the registry records
 in OpenAPI

The registry records "update" when a write that carries a principal
updates a resource, but the OpenAPI AuditEvent described action only
as create or delete, so a client following the contract would not
expect it. No endpoint updates resources yet; documenting the value
now keeps the response contract stable when one is added, instead of
surprising strict clients with a new value later.

action is now an enum of create, update and delete, and the details
description lists the updated change. The registry no longer maps
status writes to an "update_status" action: status writes never carry
a principal, so that value could not be recorded. A test runs every
registry write that takes a principal and checks that the recorded
actions are exactly the OpenAPI enum.
